            <ArticleTitle>Recognizing type 1 diabetes mellitus in children &amp; adolescents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>16-22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/01.NPR.0000516121.77126.61</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The common chief complaint of abdominal pain, nausea, and vomiting should prompt a broad differential diagnosis list. When a 17-year-old previously healthy male presented to a primary care clinic with these symptoms, it provoked a detailed workup and found a startling diagnosis of type 1 diabetes mellitus (T1DM). This article provides an overview of recognizing T1DM in children and adolescents with a thorough and diagnostic evaluation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
